## Environment Strategy

### Recommended File Structure

```
project/
├── .env                      # Local development (gitignored)
├── .env.development          # Development env (gitignored)
├── .env.staging              # Staging env (gitignored)
├── .env.production           # Production env (gitignored - only on server)
├── .env.example              # Template (committed to git)
├── .gitignore                # Git ignore rules (committed)
├── app.js
└── config/
    ├── secrets.js            # Secrets manager integration
    └── validate.js           # Secret validation
```

### .env File Loading Order (Priority)

```javascript
// Load in this order (later files override earlier ones)
1. .env                    # Default/base configuration
2. .env.local              # Local overrides (gitignored)
3. .env.{NODE_ENV}         # Environment-specific
4. .env.{NODE_ENV}.local   # Environment-specific local overrides
```

Implementation:

```javascript
const dotenv = require('dotenv');
const path = require('path');

function loadEnv() {
  const env = process.env.NODE_ENV || 'development';
  const files = [
    '.env',
    '.env.local',
    `.env.${env}`,
    `.env.${env}.local`
  ];

  files.forEach(file => {
    const configPath = path.resolve(process.cwd(), file);
    dotenv.config({ path: configPath });
  });
}

loadEnv();
```

