### 2. **A02:2021 - Cryptographic Failures**
**Finding**: No HTTPS enforcement; data transmitted in cleartext.

**Current Code**:
```javascript
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

**Issue**: No TLS/HTTPS configuration enables man-in-the-middle attacks.

**Recommendation**:
```javascript
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');

// In production, always use HTTPS
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  const options = {
    key: fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_KEY_PATH),
    cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_CERT_PATH)
  };

  https.createServer(options, app).listen(443, () => {
    console.log('HTTPS server running on port 443');
  });
} else {
  app.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log('Dev server running on port 3000');
  });
}

// Also add HTTP to HTTPS redirect middleware
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (req.header('x-forwarded-proto') !== 'https' && process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production')
    res.redirect(`https://${req.header('host')}${req.url}`);
  else
    next();
});
```

